# Rebuild dist before push

Railway serves the committed `dist/` folder. A source-only push leaves the live site on the old bundle and the old `logo.png`.

When this repo’s source, `public/`, or `index.html` has changed and the work is being committed or pushed:

1. Run `npm run build` in `india-exports-hub-53`.
2. Stage the rebuilt `dist/` (new hashed assets, deleted old assets, `dist/index.html`, and copied public files such as `dist/logo.png`).
3. Commit the source and that `dist/` together.
4. Push that commit. Do not push source without the matching production bundle.

`nixpacks.toml` and `scripts/serve-spa.mjs` are not a substitute. The live site has served a stale committed `dist/` after a source-only deploy.
